WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:04.799
Speaker 1: Today, I want to talk to you about
a topic that has become very controversial

00:00:04.799 --> 00:00:07.790
in the last few days in the United States.

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:12.830
Should doctors and scientists debate anti-vaxxers?

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:18.020
This is a question that's been raised by many
people in general in the wake of the COVID

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:19.310
19 pandemic.

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:25.880
But in addition to that, more recently, we
have seen an argument take place significantly

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:32.469
happening on social media between people like
Joe Rogan and Elon Musk and folks like Dr.

00:00:32.469 --> 00:00:39.129
Peter Hotez, who is a doctor and works on
vaccines.

00:00:39.129 --> 00:00:44.030
On the one hand, there is the argument that
doctors and scientists should not engage in

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:49.490
debates with anti-vaxxers because when a doctor
or a scientist debates an anti-vaxxer, they

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:56.430
legitimize and lend their credibility to an
anti-vaxxer for a position that doesn't actually

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:59.130
deserve legitimacy and credibility.

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:01.570
This is the position of Dr. Peter Hotez.

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:06.890
He's a doctor, a vaccine expert, professor
at the Baylor College of Medicine, and he

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:13.250
has frequently been targeted by anti-vax harassment
campaigns and even threats.

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:18.740
Hotez says debating anti-vaxxers is a losing
proposition.

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:20.560
They're not interested in facts or evidence.

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:22.460
They want to spread fear and doubt.

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:27.299
And when you engage with them in a supposed
debate, you play into their hands.

00:01:27.299 --> 00:01:31.860
You give them a platform to reach more people
with their dangerous lies and that it shouldn't

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:32.860
be done.

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:39.100
Dr. Peter Hotez also says that debating anti-vaxxers
from a practical standpoint is a waste of

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:45.600
time and a waste of resources because there's
real work that can be done educating the public,

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:47.120
explaining the benefits of vaccination.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:50.939
And he says instead of debating anti-vaxxers,
what doctors and scientists should do is just

00:01:50.939 --> 00:01:55.810
focus on communicating with people who are
hesitant about vaccines, they're unsure about

00:01:55.810 --> 00:01:56.810
vaccines.

00:01:56.810 --> 00:02:01.689
They don't have all of the information, address
their concerns with empathy and respect, and

00:02:01.689 --> 00:02:05.310
that that's a much better use of time and
resources than debating anti-vaxxers.

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:07.270
Okay, that's one side.

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:12.790
On the other hand, there are those who say
doctors and scientists should debate anti-vaxxers.

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:18.330
Now, some of the people saying that are the
anti-vaxxers, but even people who accept the

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:22.920
science and understand the science of vaccines
will sometimes say no.

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:27.340
The doctors in the scientists should debate
the anti-vaxxers because when they do that

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:28.340
they can.

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:34.129
Assuming the doctors and scientists are correct,
they will expose the flaws and the errors

00:02:34.129 --> 00:02:35.250
of the anti-vaxxers.

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:40.780
They will potentially persuade followers of
the anti-vaxxers to change their minds and

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:42.870
to come to the side of science and reason.

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:44.700
And I've heard Joe Rogan make this argument.

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:47.550
He's a popular podcast host and comedian.

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:52.340
He's been accused by some of spreading anti-vax
misinformation.

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:57.769
And he says, Listen, the anti-vax movement
has followers already.

00:02:57.769 --> 00:03:02.590
There is no downside to debating them, doctors
and scientists who are confident in their

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:07.150
arguments and that the facts are on their
side can actually do some good.

00:03:07.150 --> 00:03:14.000
When the doctors and scientists ignore or
avoid the anti-vaxxers, they miss an opportunity

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:17.010
to challenge them and to show why they are
wrong.

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:21.110
And Joe Rogan also says that when you debate
anti-vaxxers, you're respecting their freedom

00:03:21.110 --> 00:03:22.580
of speech and expression.

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:27.640
You're not participating in censoring or silencing
them, which only makes them more defiant or

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:28.640
rebellious.

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:32.820
If if nobody is going to talk to them, it
will make them more defiant and rebellious.

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:37.561
So instead of dismissing anti-vaxxers as crazy
or stupid, try to understand where they're

00:03:37.561 --> 00:03:43.180
coming from, what motivates them to reject
vaccines and meet them head on and convince

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:47.550
them with the facts that potentially will
win out.

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:49.010
Where am I on this issue?

00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:55.040
I actually don't think there is a simple or
definitive answer about whether doctors and

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:57.980
scientists should debate anti-vaxxers, and
I'll explain why.

00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:02.379
And I will say one other thing before I delve
more deeply into this.

00:04:02.379 --> 00:04:05.040
In general, when it comes to debates.

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:12.010
The person who wins is most often just like
more charismatic or a better communicator.

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:16.199
It's not necessarily the person who's factually
correct, and I think that that's a really

00:04:16.199 --> 00:04:19.550
important thing to understand, unless it's
opinion's right, which is like, okay, these

00:04:19.550 --> 00:04:22.419
are just opinions about what movie is good
or what food is good.

00:04:22.419 --> 00:04:27.190
Different scenario when we're talking about
factual stuff where there is a truth about

00:04:27.190 --> 00:04:29.240
vaccines.

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:34.000
We have to remember that in general with debate,
the better communicator, the more articulate

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.610
or charismatic person often wins.

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:41.680
And you might be a scientist with all the
facts on your side, but you just might not

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:44.130
be good in a so-called debate format.

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:46.570
And that is something that has to be considered
as well.

00:04:46.570 --> 00:04:47.570
Okay.

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:52.930
If you are talking about debating vaccines
in front of an audience, that's mostly people

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:58.340
already convinced about vaccines or supportive
of vaccines, then I don't think it's really

00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:02.850
worth the time to debate anti-vaxxers because
you're basically preaching to the choir.

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:07.980
You've got a you've got a pro-vaccine audience,
you debate an anti-vaxxer you do great.

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:09.240
You haven't convinced anyone.

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:11.030
That scenario seems like a waste of time.

00:05:11.030 --> 00:05:16.020
Instead, I would try to encourage people to
spread the word and advocate for vaccination.

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:22.889
If you've got an audience of people who are
mostly undecided or conflicted about vaccines,

00:05:22.889 --> 00:05:26.610
then it might make sense to consider debating
anti-vaxxers.

00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:32.050
And I do think in those situations, doctors
and scientists could reach a key group of

00:05:32.050 --> 00:05:36.009
people who might benefit from hearing both
sides of the argument.

00:05:36.009 --> 00:05:41.530
Assuming you have charismatic and articulate
people from from medicine and science.

00:05:41.530 --> 00:05:46.940
Doctors and scientists could appeal to the
audience and show them why vaccines are safe

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:48.160
and effective.

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:56.259
In addition to this, if the format is a structured
debate, clear rules and criteria.

00:05:56.259 --> 00:06:02.139
It benefits those with the facts on their
side, which in this case is doctors and scientists

00:06:02.139 --> 00:06:07.900
and doctors and scientists who might shy away
from these insane sort of like kill stream

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:12.860
type, insane, bonkers debates where people
just shout over each other.

00:06:12.860 --> 00:06:14.820
That doesn't seem like a good idea.

00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:21.020
If you have a more formal, structured format
with a good moderator, that also benefits

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:25.830
the side with the facts on their hands and
you're able to refute anti-vaxxers with facts

00:06:25.830 --> 00:06:26.830
and data.

00:06:26.830 --> 00:06:30.620
I think that's good chaotic, informal debate
without rules and standards.

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:35.300
I think it's not a good scenario in which
to debate anti-vaxxers.

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:41.080
You'd have you'd have you'd be at a disadvantage
in that sort of a scenario, and it's better

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:43.110
not to get dragged into that.

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:49.039
So the answer to Should doctors and scientists
debate anti-vaxxers depends on a lot of things.

00:06:49.039 --> 00:06:54.039
It depends on what is the format, how serious
are structured is the debate?

00:06:54.039 --> 00:06:55.270
Who's in the audience?

00:06:55.270 --> 00:06:56.590
What's the point?

00:06:56.590 --> 00:07:00.870
And what else could those doctors and scientists
be doing with their time?

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:05.710
As usual, these issues are not black and white,
but I want to hear from you.

00:07:05.710 --> 00:07:06.750
Let me know in a comment.

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:08.129
Let me know in an email.

00:07:08.129 --> 00:07:10.599
What do you think about this core question?

00:07:10.599 --> 00:07:18.840
Should medicine and science debate anti-vaxxers
or does it lend them the credibility and legitimacy

00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:20.330
that they should not be given?

